<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leith</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leith is the port district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firth-of-forth">Firth of Forth</a> at the mouth of the Water of Leith. For centuries Edinburgh's harbour and a centre of trade with the Baltic and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>, it was the departure point of the first Darien expedition in 1698. Merged with Edinburgh in 1920, it remains a working port and residential area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leith.jpg" alt="Leith" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RuthAS · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rth_Edin_Leith_.Forth.Fife_26.10.11_edited-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
